An FPD pellicle is a thin, transparent membrane mounted above a photomask. It helps prevent particles from settling directly on the mask surface by keeping contamination away from the focal plane of the exposure system. This protection is important because even small particles can create defects that are transferred to display substrates during exposure. Pellicle performance depends on optical transparency, mechanical stability, membrane uniformity and compatibility with the manufacturing environment.

